# Redoubt LW-M7-42: login fields inside open shadow roots reach Android
# Autofill.
#
# GeckoViewAutoFillChild registers fields with the app (the "Add" message that
# becomes the ViewStructure an AutofillService sees) from three places only:
# DOMFormHasPassword and DOMInputPasswordAdded, which are not composed and so
# never leave a shadow root, and scanDocument's querySelectorAll, which stops
# at shadow roots. onFocus then only resolves fields that were registered
# (plus upstream's datalist fallback). A login whose inputs live in open
# shadow roots (reddit.com/login: faceplate-text-input, name=username
# autocomplete="username webauthn", name=password) is therefore invisible:
# focusing the field sends no Focus, Android sends no fill request, and every
# password manager stays silent. Stock Fenix 157 behaves the same.
#
# The patch adds one more fallback in onFocus, next to the datalist one. When
# the focused element is unregistered and is
#   * an <input> in a shadow tree whose shadow roots are all open, and
#   * a login field: a password field (hasBeenTypePassword); or a
#     username-type field (LoginHelper.isUsernameFieldType) whose
#     shadow-inclusive FormLike (below) holds a password field, and that
#     LoginHelper infers to be a username or email field (autocomplete
#     username/webauthn/email, or the words in its attributes or label) or
#     LoginManagerChild's own heuristics (_getFormFields) pick as the
#     username. The password requirement matches upstream, which registers
#     only forms with a password field: a newsletter or checkout email field
#     with no password field beside it stays unregistered, and the username
#     heuristics are not run for it,
# it builds a FormLike rooted where FormLikeFactory would root it (the closest
# <form> across shadow hosts, else the document element), whose elements also
# include the fields of every open shadow root under that root, and passes it
# to addElement. addElement runs LoginManagerChild's username heuristics over
# those elements (LoginManagerChild's own LoginForm for the field only sees
# the light DOM), so the username field still gets the "username" hint.
#
# Not changed: light-DOM fields (returned early, byte-for-byte the upstream
# path), closed shadow roots and UA-widget roots (Element.shadowRoot is null
# for both, and a field under one is rejected), non-login inputs (search, OTP,
# email or text fields with no password field in their FormLike, anything
# else), null-principal documents. No new network, no new prefs.
# Cost: one DOM walk when an unregistered login-like field in a shadow root is
# focused; once registered, later focuses hit the cache.
#
# Known limit: if the same page also has a formless light-DOM password field
# that upstream registers after ours, the document root is re-sent with
# upstream's light-DOM element list, and the app's structure can lose the
# shadow fields for that page. Not seen on any page tested.
#
# Test page and emulator evidence: docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-42/autofill-shadow-dom/.
#
