+  /**
+   * Redoubt: if aField is a login field inside an open shadow root that the
+   * events above never registered, return a FormLike for it whose elements
+   * include the fields of every open shadow root under its root element
+   * (the closest <form> across shadow boundaries, else the document).
+   * Returns null for anything else, which keeps upstream behaviour: fields in
+   * the light DOM, fields in a closed shadow root (or under one), and fields
+   * that are not login fields.
+   *
+   * A login field here is a password field, or a username-type field in a
+   * FormLike whose (shadow-inclusive) elements contain a password field and
+   * that is either inferred by LoginHelper to be a username or email field
+   * (autocomplete username/webauthn/email, or "username"/"email" in its
+   * attributes or label) or picked by LoginManagerChild's own heuristics as
+   * the username. Upstream registers only forms that hold a password field,
+   * so an email field with no password field beside it (newsletter,
+   * checkout) is not a login field.
+   *
+   * @param aField Focused element.
+   */
+  _formLikeForShadowLoginField(aField) {
